{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor v in s['interpretations']:\n    if v['id'].startswith('fedb7ea'):\n        print(json.dumps(v,indent=1))\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"id\": \"fedb7ea2467845edb2dcd2326f174dec-interpretation-0\",\n \"investigation_id\": \"cb86a487ef704d8dbb90189aa23abcfc-question-1\",\n \"experiment_id\": null,\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"nodehost-sync-read\",\n  \"nodehost-read-index-api\",\n  \"nodehost-linearizable-read\",\n  \"nodehost-read-index-helper\",\n  \"node-read-entry\",\n  \"nodehost-request-state-mapping\",\n  \"request-local-read-guard\",\n  \"nodehost-read-local-node\"\n ],\n \"executions\": {},\n \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n \"defect_claim\": null,\n \"rationale\": \"The captured source locates the client surface of the parent question's asserted defect. NodeHost.SyncRead passes the caller context to linearizableRead, which reaches the internal readIndex helper and node.read; node.read registers the read through pendingReadIndex.read and returns the RequestState, and the helper marks the node ready so the read is sent. NodeHost.ReadIndex, the API documented for the two-step pattern, calls the same helper and returns that RequestState, and ReadLocalNode guards on the ready-to-read flag that only a completed batch sets. The wait path maps results uniformly: a completed result returns normally, a timeout result or an expired caller context returns ErrTimeout, a dropped result returns ErrClusterNotReady, and rejected, terminated or aborted results map to their own errors. Combined with the parent receipts, in which a reply carrying another request's context left the admitted batch at index zero after a valid ready index was applied, the client-visible endpoint for an affected follower or observer read is ErrTimeout at the caller's deadline rather than a completion, and it is distinguishable from the dropped path that returns ErrClusterNotReady. This account is source-only and makes no independent defect claim; the defect judgment and its receipts remain in the parent question.\",\n \"answers\": {},\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"cb86a487ef704d8dbb90189aa23abcfc-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"SyncRead and ReadIndex both register their read through the same pending-read batch, and the shared result mapping returns ErrTimeout for a timeout result or an expired caller context and ErrClusterNotReady only for a dropped result.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The public funnel is source-traced only; no retained execution drives NodeHost.SyncRead or NodeHost.ReadIndex through a substituted reply.\",\n  \"An expired caller context returns ErrTimeout from the context branch itself, so an ErrTimeout observed by a client does not by itself prove the batch was stranded.\",\n  \"ReadLocalNode panics when the ready flag is unset, so a client that ignores completion fails loudly rather than reading unconfirmed data, which is the documented contract.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"This is a source-only account of the public read APIs; it does not execute NodeHost or the transport.\",\n  \"It does not measure how long a caller waits, because the wait is bounded by the caller's own context and the node's timeout tick.\",\n  \"It covers the documented consumption pattern only and does not survey application code that might poll the RequestState differently.\",\n  \"The asynchronous ReadIndex result codes are mapped as read; no retained receipt exercises each branch.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"\",\n \"failure_attribution\": null,\n \"operation_id\": \"fedb7ea2467845edb2dcd2326f174dec\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns = json.load(open('state.json'))\nrec = [v for v in s['interpretations'] if v['id'].startswith('fedb7ea')][0]\nkeep = ['investigation_id','experiment_id','source_ids','executions','conclusion','defect_claim','rationale','answers','knowledge','counterevidence','limitations','joint_history','failure_attribution']\nu = {k: rec[k] for k in keep if k in rec}\nanchor = \\\"and ReadLocalNode guards on the ready-to-read flag that only a completed batch sets.\\\"\nadd = (\\\" Both entry points require a caller-supplied timeout: linearizableRead takes the timeout from the context and converts it to the node's timeout tick, and node.read refuses before registration when the node is uninitialized or is a witness, so a witness client never reaches the pending batch while an uninitialized node is rejected with ErrClusterNotReady.\\\")\nassert anchor in u['rationale']\nu['rationale'] = u['rationale'].replace(anchor, anchor + add, 1)\nu['knowledge'] = list(u['knowledge']) + [{\n  \\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"6407b19cd3ee4277baeb54f917fdc1da-knowledge-0\\\",\n  \\\"revision\\\": 1,\n  \\\"assertion\\\": \\\"The checker-chain entry records the caller-timeout requirement and the witness and uninitialized-node rejections that precede pending-batch registration.\\\"\n}]\nu['limitations'] = list(u['limitations']) + [\n  \\\"The affected endpoint is confined to non-witness members because node.read rejects a witness with ErrInvalidOperation before registering the read; observer reads travel the observer's own forwarding path measured in the parent receipts.\\\"\n]\nout = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Refine the client-surface account with the checked call order and its two admission guards. Node read entry takes a caller-supplied timeout and rejects an uninitialized node and a